nodecode-acedatacloud is a rewrite of AceDataCloud's AceDataCloud/AceDataCloudModelProviderHermes:
https://github.com/AceDataCloud/AceDataCloudModelProviderHermes
commit 568763ee21fe081562bb9bcd91e7323f8f81d6ff
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Ace Data Cloud (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the provider itself, as one Nodecode cell. __init__.py's profile --
name, display name, signup address, key variable, base URL, chat_completions
transport and its two models -- became the catalog row in PROVIDER.LISP and
CELL.LISP, which is the one shape every Nodecode reader takes a provider in: the
picker, /models, lane resolution, /connect's key check. Its fetch_models
override, which narrows the account's shared model list to gpt-4.1 and
gpt-4.1-mini and falls back to those two when the catalog is unreachable,
became LISTING-ROWS and LISTING in CELL.LISP. plugin.yaml's requires_env
became the section and the :CREDENTIAL hook, which reads
ACEDATACLOUD_API_KEY and never falls through to another family's variable.

Left out: the Hermes-only halves of the original, because Nodecode has its own
for each. The plugin.yaml manifest, the hermes plugins validate/doctor gates
and the README's picker screenshot become the cell contract, the cell's own
test system and the .asd :properties entry; the signup_url's referral
parameters have no Nodecode seam (its picker opens no signup link) and are
left out rather than carried as dead data; and the CI scripts (the published
catalog acceptance run and the unittest suite) are not ported, since the cell
tests its own behaviour offline. The original's two model rows carry no
pricing, and the rewrite invents none: Ace bills from its own balance.
